                                </zone-style>
                              </zone>
                              <zone fixed-size='264' h='15111' id='2173' is-fixed='true' name='Intervals' w='99000' x='500' y='24375'>
                                <layout-cache type-h='cell' type-w='fixed' />
                                <zone-style>
                                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                                </zone-style>
                              </zone>
                              <zone fixed-size='150' h='8777' id='2174' is-fixed='true' type-v2='empty' w='99000' x='500' y='39486'>
                                <zone-style>
                                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                                </zone-style>
                              </zone>
                              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='5388' id='2134' type-v2='text' w='99000' x='500' y='48263'>
                                <formatted-text>
                                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>What are confidence intervals?</run>
                                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                                  <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>The </run>
                                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>confidence interval </run>
                                  <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b'>is a range that we expect our sample to fall between 95% of the times if we run the experiment again. In other words - if we run the experiment again and again many times, in 95% of the times we would get a result that lies inside the confidence interval.</run>
                                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                                </formatted-text>
                                <zone-style>
                                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                                </zone-style>
                              </zone>
                              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='7000' id='2122' type-v2='text' w='99000' x='500' y='53651'>
                                <formatted-text>
                                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Why do we not show confidence intervals for CUPED-adjusted KPIs?</run>
                                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                                  <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>CUPED is a method of KPI manipulation. Generally, we use the pre-test data that we have about the users in both groups in order to remove pre-existing differences between the groups and measure only the changes that are the result of the experiment itself (for more details, please check the friendly guide linked above).</run>
                                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                                  <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>Due to this shifting of the KPIs, the significance analysis is done on shifted KPIs with shifted means</run>
                                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                                  <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>Showing confidence intervals for these shifted KPIs will not say anything about the KPIs themselves.</run>
                                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                                  <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='8'>To avoid confusion, we do not show confidence intervals for CUPED-adjusted means.</run>
                                </formatted-text>
                                <zone-style>
                                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                                </zone-style>
                              </zone>
                              <zone h='15170' id='2172' type-v2='empty' w='99000' x='500' y='60651'>
                                <zone-style>
                                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
